<title>SWEDEN: TABLE - Atlas Copco profit up 10 pct H1.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Atlas Copco profit up 10 pct H1.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish industrial engineer Atlas Copco on Wednesday posted its results for the six months ending June 30, 1997.</p>
<p>					(million crowns unless stated)</p>
<p> Profit after fin items		 1,719  vs  1,567</p>
<p> Turnover				  13,784  vs 12,374</p>
<p> Earnings per share (SKR)	     5.80   vs  5.57</p>
<p> Operating costs			 12,079  vs 10,883</p>
<p> Operating profit			 1,705  vs  1,491</p>
<p> Net financial items			 14  vs     76</p>
<p> Tax					    639  vs    531</p>
<p> Minorities		     CHARGE     16  vs     13 CHARGE</p>
<p> Net profit				 1,064  vs  1,023</p>
<p>NOTE -- Atlas Copco was expected to post a profit after financial items of 1.55 billion crowns for the first half of 1997, a Reuters poll of 10 analysts found.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
